{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And a quarter-hin of wine for the one lamb as a drink-offering.</b> Our Rabbi Hananel, of blessed memory, wrote: once he bent down to perform the libation, the deputy [priest] waved the flags and Ben Arza struck the cymbal, and the Levites would break into song. When they reached a blowing-section they blew, and the people would bow down at every blowing-section and at every single blast they would bow down — and this is what is written explicitly (II Chronicles 29:28): ״וכל הקהל משתחוים והשיר משורר והחצצרות מחצצרים הכל עד לכלות העולה וככלות להעלות כרעו המלך וכל הנמצאים אתו וישתחוו״, and the Levites would sing in the Sanctuary over the sacrifices every single day. The song they would say on the first day of the week (Psalms 24:1): ״לה' הארץ ומלואה״ — and this corresponds to the creation of the world, of which it is written (Genesis 1:3) ״והארץ היתה תהו ובהו״; and ״ויבא מלך הכבוד״ corresponds to ״ויאמר אלהים יהי אור״ — for the glory of the Shekhinah is a great light. On the second day (Psalms 48:1–2): ״שיר מזמור לבני קרח גדול ה' ומהולל מאד בעיר אלהינו״ etc., and it is written (ibid.): ״אלהים בארמנותיה נודע למשגב״ — that He separated between the Holy and the Holy of Holies, between the priests' court and the Israelites' court, which are 'her palaces'; this corresponds to the second day, on which the upper waters were separated from the lower, as it is said (Genesis 1:6): ״ויהי מבדיל בין מים למים״. On the third day (Psalms 82): ״מזמור לאסף אלהים נצב בעדת אל״, and it is written (ibid.): ״שפטו דל ויתום עני ורש הצדיקו״ — meaning that the judges gather to judge each and every one as is fitting for him; and this corresponds to ״יקוו המים״, in connection with which it is written ״ועץ עושה פרי למינו״ (ibid.), and (ibid. v. 7) ״אכן כאדם תמותון״ — meaning: I created the Garden of Eden for the human being, and once he sinned he was expelled from there — so too you. On the fourth day (Psalms 94): ״אל נקמות ה'״ — corresponding to the worshippers of the sun and the moon, which were created on the fourth day; and it is written (Deuteronomy 32:41): ״אשיב נקם לצרי״. On the fifth day (Psalms 81): ״למנצח על הגתית לאסף הרנינו לאלהים עוזנו״, and it is written in it: ״המעלך מארץ מצרים״, and Pharaoh was likened to the sea-monster (תנין), as it is said (Ezekiel 29:3): ״התנים הגדול״, and on that same day it is written (Genesis 1:21): ״ויברא אלהים את התנינים הגדולים״. On the sixth day (Psalms 93:1): ״ה' מלך גאות לבש״ — corresponding to the creation of the human being, as it is said (Genesis 1:26): ״בצלמנו כדמותנו״, and ״וירדו״; and He alone, may His name be exalted, is exalted above all the exalted and rules over all who rule, and it is further written (Psalms 93:1): ״אף תכון תבל בל תמוט״. On the seventh day (Psalms 92): ״מזמור שיר ליום השבת״, and it is written in it: ״שתולים בבית ה'״. And it is possible that there is in these songs more than what we have mentioned of the proofs that they correspond to the days of Genesis. Thus far the language of the master, of blessed memory."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "Rabbeinu Bahya cites R. Hananel's list of the daily Levitical songs mapped to the days of Creation; the citations and verse-linkages are reproduced exactly as he gives them, including the slight misattribution of Genesis 1:3 (which is actually v. 3 of the chapter but contains ויאמר אלהים יהי אור, while והארץ היתה תהו ובהו is Gen 1:2)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:39.183528062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}